 original  and this goes all the way down to the  collectibles there were a lot more side  stories going on  missing agents and other recordings that  you could piece together to expand on  the main story  however there is one thing i'd love to  see them continue doing  in the original game we were presented  with the main storyline and that was  pretty much it  we had a few bits and pieces added when  they opened up the west side pair but  nothing substantial  the division ii story has evolved over  time where i think they went wrong  is the way they did it through seasons  after the first manhunt or two  a lot of people were sick of them and  missed out on the future additions  the other thing is that they only did it  through the collectibles the comms  most people would have preferred a  cutscene or two but i like the way  they've continued on with the story  although maybe not told the way everyone  would like it there has been a lot more  happen than in the division one  however i still don't forgive them for  what they did with aaron kina  speaking of which this is another area  that i've noticed people aren't a fan of  the twists and turns the good guys  turning bad  it seems that a lot of people would  prefer straightforward good guys versus  bad guy's story  with the division especially the  division two takes it from more of a  the bad guys aren't completely bad and  the good aren't exactly good  i actually like this it adds a bit more  depth makes it feel  grittier but having said all that if i  had to choose a favorite  it would be the way in which the first  game was told and to be fair  it would always be that way regardless  of how the division two turned out  and however they tell the story in the  future the division one is the thing  that started it all  there is too much history there and over  time the nostalgia  will only grow  from a gameplay point of view the  division 2 is smoother and a little more  fast paced  but when looking at the end game it's  still quite far behind  the sequel has a number of quality of  life additions that made the division 1  feel a little bit of a chore  especially when it came to inventory and  having to restock ammo one at a time  but the main thing that sets them apart  is the pvp  it's like they haven't even bothered  with it in the second game to be fair i  saw the same complaints from the same  people in the first game  but the division 2 certainly didn't help  calm the noise  summing up in my opinion the division 1  is more complete when it comes to game  modes and in-game  but the division 2 is better to play in  almost every other aspect  so tell me where do you stand with the  two games what do you like about each of  them  anyway thanks for watching and i'll  catch in the next one cheers  [Music]  okay

